      "title": "Public network access is enabled by default",
      "resource": "azurerm_mysql_server.changeme_simple_mysql_server",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "explanation": "The resource does not explicitly set `public_network_access_enabled` to false. By default, Azure MySQL servers allow public network access, exposing the database to the internet unless restricted by firewall rules (which are absent here)."
    },
    {
      "check_id": "CKV_AZURE_54",
      "title": "Minimum TLS version not enforced",
      "resource": "azurerm_mysql_server.changeme_simple_mysql_server",
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "explanation": "The `minimal_tls_version` attribute is not set. While SSL enforcement is on, older TLS versions (1.0/1.1) may still be accepted depending on the platform defaults. Explicitly setting it to 'TLS1_2' ensures modern encryption standards."
    },
    {
      "check_id": "CKV_AZURE_94",
      "title": "Geo-redundant backups not enabled",
      "resource": "azurerm_mysql_server.changeme_simple_mysql_server",
      "severity": "LOW",
      "explanation": "The `geo_redundant_backup_enabled` attribute is not set to true. This means backups are stored locally within the region only, increasing risk of data loss in a regional disaster."
    }
  ],
  "patched_code": "resource \"azurerm_mysql_server\" \"changeme_simple_mysql_server\" {\n  name                = \"changeme-simple-mysql-database-name\"\n  resource_group_name = azurerm_resource_group.changeme_simple_mysql_server_resource_group.name\n  location            = azurerm_resource_group.changeme_simple_mysql_server_resource_group.location\n  storage_mb          = \"5120\"\n  sku_name            = \"B_Gen5_1\"\n  version             = \"8.0\"\n  administrator_login          = \"changemeadmin\"\n  administrator_login_password = \"ch4ng3m3-A@Â£$%^&\"\n  ssl_enforcement_enabled      = true\n  public_network_access_enabled = false\n  minimal_tls_version           = \"TLS1_2\"\n  geo_redundant_backup_enabled  = true\n}",
